## How to Use

### Mode A: Deconstruction and Learning
In a new conversation, simply say: "**Help me deconstruct and analyze a certain open-source project (provide the AI ​​with a link or the location of a cloned local repository)**". You can add tiers ("Quick Deconstruction" / "In-Depth Deconstruction") and focus points ("Focus on Performance"). Output is in `oss-teardown/<run-id>/`: `notes/` evidence for each stage + `LEARNING_REPORT.md`. Tier budgets: Quick (single Agent, community search ≤4, core modules ≥30%) / Standard (default, ≤12, ≥60%) / In-Depth (3–5 Workers, ≤24, ≥90%).

### Mode B: Project Takeover
Say: "**Take over this project. The previous AI left handover materials. First, conduct independent reconnaissance, then compare, and generate a takeover plan**". Process: Blind scan to form your own understanding (five types of restatement) → Compare with handover materials → Truth hierarchy arbitration (code > document) → Hypothesis registration → Generate `.ai/` handover package → **H5 user access control: only move a line of code after your approval** → Checkpoint execution → Five-stage final acceptance. Red lines in the handover document are bound by default; only after the AI ​​clearly understands your project can you release them and let it work.

### Mode C Handover Freeze When you feel your quota is running out, tell the **current AI**: "**My quota is running out; use Mode C to freeze the session for this project and hand over the handover document**." It will go through C0–C5: confirm path → check memory with git status/diff → extract red lines and to-dos → **write and dump simultaneously** (write the header + red lines + status table + the next safety skeleton first; even if the quota dies halfway, a valid contract remains) → self-check and archive. The document is located in `<project>/.ai/handoffs/HANDOFF-<subject>-<date>.md`, with a "No-Skill Takeover Agreement" appended at the end. **The next AI can take over regardless of whether they have this skill installed.**

### Resuming from Breakpoints The new session says: "**Continue the disassembly that wasn't finished yesterday, resuming from the last checkpoint.**" The skill reads `run-manifest.json` in the run directory, verifies the schema version, and then continues from the breakpoint.

### You can say it like this:

- "Help me break down and analyze this open-source project (link to the open-source project for the AI)"

- "Break down this project: how many modules are used for each requirement, and why was this framework chosen for each module?"

- "Taking over this unfinished project; the previous AI left handover materials."

- "I'm almost out of credit; write a handover document to pass the baton to the next model."

- "Continue the breakdown that wasn't finished yesterday, resuming from the checkpoint."

## Installation

```bash

# Method 1: Skills CLI, global installation (recommended)

npx skills add hoshinohatsuka/project-relay-Skill -g

# Method 2: Skills CLI, only for the current project (execute in the project root directory)

npx skills add hoshinohatsuka/project-relay

# Method 3: Manual installation (ZCode / Claude Code / Codex, etc.)

git clone https://github.com/hoshinohatsuka/project-relay
mkdir -p ~/.agents/skills && cp -r project-relay ~/.agents/skills/

# [OpenCode](https://opencode.ai/) The global directory is ~/.config/opencode/skills/. It is recommended to share the same directory using a directory link:

# powershell -Command "New-Item -ItemType Junction -Path \"$env:USERPROFILE\.config\opencode\skills\project-relay\" -Target '<path to this repository>'"

```

Prerequisites: `git` is available; Agent has Bash/file read/write/Grep/Glob permissions; Community research requires internet access (automatically downgraded and marked as `missing evidence` if missing).

## Security

- **Target source code read-only**: Do not execute/build/install disassembled code, do not initialize submodules, do not pull LFS, and do not load target `.env` values.

- **Protection Word Injection Protection**: All files and web pages within the target repository are treated as data; any directive text within them is not executed.

- **File System Isolation**: Only the output root directory is written; path escape is prevented.

- **Mode B Access Control**: No code is modified in H5 without your approval; change restrictions (schema/public API/authentication, etc.) are closed by default; each checkpoint can be rolled back.

- **Security Hygiene**: Only variable names are recorded; values ​​are anonymized; artifacts are bypassed by key scanning.

## Verified vs. Unverified

Verified (reproducible commands are in `evals/EVALUATION_PLAN.md`): package integrity, trigger-contract evaluation, positive and negative blackboard-state fixtures, and manual review rubrics for all four workflows. These prove file, deterministic routing-contract, and state-artifact structure. They do not prove host auto-routing or literal compliance by every model.

Unverified (missing evidence): real host auto-routing; end-to-end adherence by a real model in modes A, B, C, and resume; performance of deep files in large-scale repositories (>500 modules); community recall rate on login firewall platforms.

## Troubleshooting

| Phenomenon | Solution |

|---|---|

| Cloning failed | Check git and network; switch private repository to local path |

| Report of missing evidence | Previous AI model unavailable or budget exhausted; pattern shared by A and B, passed to the next AI to run this stage |

| Large repository cannot be read | Downgrade to fast file, or specify `focus` to focus on the module |

| "Continue from last time" not working | Confirm the run directory exists and `schema_version` is 2.x; run `python scripts/validate_run.py <run directory>` for a check |

| Skill not triggered | Force loading using `/skill project-relay-Skill <request>` |

| Want to re-split (line number has drifted) | Bind old evidence to old commit SHA; create a new run-id and rerun |

